.TH FERRENTD 1 "2026-11-19" "ferrentd 0.1.0" "Ferrent"
.SH NAME
ferrentd \- Ferrent BitTorrent daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ferrentd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ferrentd
is the headless BitTorrent daemon. It listens on a TLS gRPC socket, keeps the
torrent state in a redb database and restores fastresume data after a restart.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The daemon reads
.I /etc/ferrent/config.toml
by default. The file contains:
.PP
.nf
data_dir = "/var/lib/ferrent"
bind = "127.0.0.1:50051"
token_file = "/etc/ferrent/token"
.fi
.PP
The token file must be readable by the
.B ferrent
user (mode 0640, owner root:ferrent). The TLS certificate is created on first
start in
.IR data_dir .
.PP
Environment variables
.BR FERRENT_DATA_DIR ,
.BR FERRENT_BIND ,
.BR FERRENT_TOKEN
and
.B FERRENT_CONFIG
override the file values.
.SH SERVICE
.B systemctl start ferrentd
starts the daemon. The unit waits up to 120 seconds for a clean shutdown so
that fastresume data can be saved.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ferrent/config.toml
configuration
.TP
.I /etc/ferrent/token
API token (generated on first install)
.TP
.I /var/lib/ferrent
state.redb, TLS material and torrent data
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ferrent-cli (1),
.BR ferrent-gui (1)
